a13caa4885f547c8d206265b031ba7649e539fd9:docs/SPIN_HALF_CUBIC_ICE_INFRARED_FORWARD_REPLAY_RECOVERY_BOUNDARY_NOTE_2026-09-05.md:21:For gaps g=(g6,g12,g20), the contrast matrix has rows (-1,1,0) and (-1,0,1). The current diagnostic uses D Sigma D^T, requiring positive definiteness when it is inverted. The full Sigma must be positive semidefinite and agree with the printed standard errors within their eight-decimal rounding tolerance. Genuine RK rows have identical forward estimates and rank-one covariance, so the zero-contrast identity is checked without inverting its zero covariance.
